From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:04:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] yblod-54: move the fork's strings to ids 45000 to 45999

The fork's 79 Dolby Vision strings used #40810-#40925, directly above
Kodi's newest string (#40804 at the pinned commit, #40806 on master
today), and the VRR patch (yblod-36) took #13484 and #36059 from
Kodi's own ranges, which Kodi master already uses. The next Kodi update
would have given those ids two meanings.

Kodi's core strings use nothing above #40806 (master 7ad52a09); add-ons
and skins use 30000-32999. Move every fork string to the 45000 block:
#13484 -> #45000, #36059 -> #45001, #408xx/#409xx -> +4200 (#45010 to
#45125), and give #13484 and #36059 back to Kodi's empty ranges. The
settings (settings.xml, linux.xml) and Estuary's player information
panel use the new ids.

WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp and DVPrivateVulkan.cpp still ask for eight
of these strings (#40810, #40812-#40814, #40900, #40901, #40920,
#40925) by their old ids, so those entries stay, marked, until that code
uses the new ones.
